    std::cout << "Enter your choice (r/p/s): ";
    std::cin >> playerChoice;

    playerChoice = tolower(playerChoice);

    int player;
    if (playerChoice == 'r') player = 0;
    else if (playerChoice == 'p') player = 1;
    else if (playerChoice == 's') player = 2;
    else {
        std::cout << "Invalid input! Try again.\n";
        continue; // ⬅ This goes back to start of do-while loop
    }

    // Rest of game logic...
} while (playAgain == 'y');
```

### 🔁 So What Does `continue;` Do Here?
- If user enters anything other than `'r'`, `'p'`, or `'s'`, the game skips all remaining logic and **asks for input again**.

